  "experiment_id": "2026-09-24-e27b-long-prefill-cadence",
  "title": "E27b: the E27 prefill cadence applied to long prefills only",
  "outcome": "superseded",
  "outcome_detail": "Accepted by the owner as a candidate and promoted inside E27c. Against the frozen E27 medians: C4 per-stream TTFT -27.2%, code decode +4.5%, C2 +2.8%, prose +2.1%, C1 end-to-end -4.0% (treated as noise by the owner), prefill and replay within -2.1% to +1.0%. The arriving request reaches its first token 2-54% sooner with running agents; the time those agents lose is unchanged. Several long contexts arriving together still stall the first stream (6.1 tok/s), as on E27.",
